        "text": {
          "content": "pattern: raes-library-pattern\nversion: 1\nid: observable-study-conditions\nsurface: study\nrequirement_refs:\n- AUT-806\nsource_refs:\n- examples/scenarios/satcom-release-poisoning.sdl.yaml\n- docs/decisions/adrs/adr-073-scoring-reward-language-scope.md\nsummary: Represent study-style examples through propositions, assertions, and explicit\n  probe bindings while keeping graded scoring in the experiment/evaluator plane.\nintent: 'Make study-like examples reusable by connecting participant activity to backend-neutral\n  propositions, assertions, evidence requirements, and workflow protocol. Graded scoring,\n  reward, and interpretation live in the experiment/evaluator plane (experiment-*\n  contracts) per ADR-073, not in the SDL.\n\n  '\nuse_when:\n- A study needs a repeatable, observable definition of participant success.\n- Reviewers need to see how evidence and a probe binding support an asserted proposition.\nauthoring_steps:\n- Define a typed proposition with grounded property semantics and finite subjects.\n- Declare the evidence requirement needed for observed-state truth.\n- Bind a condition probe to the proposition when an executable check is needed.\n- Reference a postcondition or invariant assertion from objective success.\n- Drive the objective from a workflow protocol step.\n- Carry any graded scoring or reward in the experiment/evaluator plane, not the SDL.\nvalidation:\n- command: parse_sdl_file\n  expected: proposition, assertion, evidence, objective, and workflow references resolve\n    with no removed scoring surfaces.\nname: changed\n",
